{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["And repays them that hate Him to His face — He pays them back for their sins." "To His face — in his lifetime, to him and to his children, up to the fourth generation; this is: He will not delay — either in his lifetime or up to the fourth generation. This is its plain sense, and this is the measure of good far exceeding the measure of punishment: for sins He does not punish beyond the fourth generation, but the recompense of kindnesses — even though they sin for a hundred generations, one righteous man's righteousness stands even for the last generation of the thousandth generation, for him to be found whole."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {1 "Reading רביעי/רבעים as variants of 'fourth generation'; the text appears to alternate between רביעי and רבעים, likely orthographic variants for the same concept."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:28.182208567Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}